WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:08.980
I got this uh... tattoo... couple years ago.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.460
Maybe two years.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.780
It's not the best tattoo.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.880
'Cause... For example, if you roll up- If I roll up my sleeve...

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.820
Kinda looks like two balls hanging out.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:21.720
[laughs]

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.380
You may be familiar with it already.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.380
It's uh... It's a figurine made by KAWS.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.360
Which used to sell for like 50 bucks, but I think now they're like two grand.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.120
If you're lucky enough to find one.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.920
'Cause KAWS has gotten so popular.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.280
And I was really worried when I got it, 'cause I thought... Maybe even too popular.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.760
And yeah... In some ways uh...

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.160
I was right.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:43.820
*laughs*

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:45.980
I cringe every time.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.940
Another reason you might recognize it previously is because, uhm...

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.120
The figurine is a variation of Astro Boy.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.600
Which is a '50s, '60s Japanese super hero.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:03.700
And if you search Astro Boy on YouTube, you'll find a picture typically where he's fist towards the sky with a smile.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:04.800
Uhm...

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:07.220
Striking that super hero pose.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:13.660
But in this variation, Astro Boy is uh... leaned forward. He's uh, covering his face.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:15.140
In shame.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:21.520
And we see Astro Boy in a way that typically would never happen, at least in the original manga.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.880
And uh... And I think when you're a character that people look up to...

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:30.180
It's not typically to show certain types of emotions.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:38.140
For me, seeing Astro Boy in a way that's so... unlike the typical way that people usually perceive him...

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.360
I know it's a little cheesy.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.940
Made me think it's okay to not always be the way you're typically seen by people.

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:44.440
[laughs]

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:50.080
Although we might never actually see it, everyone gets down every once in a while.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:54.180
Everyone feels the way as good 'ole Astro Boy feels.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.460
No matter who you are.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:56.400
Although...

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.300
We might not actually ever see it.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.120
Everyone gets down from time to time.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.180
Even if you're a super hero... like Astro Boy.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.440
So it's my favorite tattoo.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:18.460
I'm back, and uh... I feel so much better to be back already.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:23.140
If you don't know, I took some time off to work on Scare Pewdiepie Season 2.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.940
The sh- My- My own show.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:29.480
It should be coming out early next year.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.540
It was so much more intense.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:33.260
Way more than I ever expected.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.900
This season really steps it up so much.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:43.160
And I really- I feel really confident that you guys, you bros... Anyone really will really enjoy watching it.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.800
'Cause we had such a blast filming it.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.480
And I think each episode on this one is really strong.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:54.820
I'm probably not supposed to say this, but Jacksepticeye is sort of a villain of the show.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:03:00.560
And he flew in the last couple days to shoot some trailer stuff with me.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.740
We got ot do some Kung Fu moves.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.860
We got to ride a motorcycle.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:08.140
And uh... It's just awesome. It was so much fun.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:11.540
I worked every single day that week, but it was totally worth it.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.440
And in the finale, we kinda went head to head.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:22.080
In the end, we were both kinda up on the stage in front of a... everyone that worked on the show, and it was just a really, really awesome moment.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.540
So memorable for me.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:24.440
Uh...

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:29.040
Don't want to spoil anything, but I was just really happy Jack was there, and it was cool to share that moment with him.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.780
I'm so excited for you guys to watch this season.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:35.420
I wanna say a huge thanks to everyone who worked on the production.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:37.620
They obviously worked ten times harder than I did.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:41.380
And... I just really appreciate all the hard work that went into it.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:45.540
So everyone that worked on it, you know who you are, thank you.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:49.920
All the guests that came and went on the show, everyone was so good.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.520
We didn't have a single bad guest.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:55.880
Some even flew over to L.A. just to be part of the show, which I really, really appreciate.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:56.640
And uhm...

00:03:58.800 --> 00:03:59.840
Just thank you.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:04.480
Thanks again to Brad and Michael for flying over with me and being part of me while I did this.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:07.760
They were huge help, and I really appreciate their support.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.480
Same with Marzia, of course, for supporting me these three weeks and being by my side.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:18.220
She obviously took time off her... what she was doing to be with me, and uh... I really appreciate that.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:24.980
But also... thanks to you on my last video, all the support was just incredible.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:28.060
And it means a lot that you were all there for me when I needed it.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:32.640
And uh... everyone that contacted me and wrote me to make sure I was okay.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:34.000
I'm really fine.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.920
I really have... [laughs]

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.260
I really have the best life ever.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:42.080
I have no reason to complain or "Oh, boo-hoo I'm stressed."

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.880
But uh... I think it's normal to get down every once in while.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:47.240
I'm just so happy to be back.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.780
I'm excited to make videos again.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:53.160
And... uh... I'll be back tomorrow with another one.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.360
Edgar... Edgar, come here.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:57.320
I'm finally back with Edgar.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:59.080
[kisses Edgar]

00:04:59.240 --> 00:04:59.880
[laughs]

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.560
[dog's mind] "I missed you, Poods. I missed you."

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.340
Edgar's gotten fat now.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:08.640
The one that took care of him clearly fed him too much.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:09.920
[laughs]

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:12.140
I don't think Edgar has any objections to that.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.060
So yeah.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:18.540
Don't mean to keep saying thank you, but thanks for all your support.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:20.360
Thanks for waiting for me when I'm gone.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:28.400
I really appreciate that I have an audience that uh... support what I do in a way that... is more than just videos almost.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:29.740
If that makes sense.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:33.040
Really kept me going throughout these days, and I appreciate you.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:33.620
[kisses]

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:36.740
So as always, we're gonna end it with a brofist.

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:41.140
Thanks for leaving a like. I guess I gotta beg for that now that YouTube changed the system.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:44.200
And I'll see you bros in the next video.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.240
Stay awesome, bros.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:49.680
I almost... How could I forget?

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.820
I haven't met Slippy in three weeks.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.240
I hope he's alive.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:55.280
Aww...

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:56.980
Slippy...

00:05:57.980 --> 00:05:59.660
Aww...

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:02.480
How you doing, buddy?

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.300
I missed you.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:07.000
Don't shit.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:07.880
How you doing?

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:08.800
My little cheeseburger.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:10.280
Oh.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.440
You gonna shit?

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:15.260
Are you pissed that I- Oh, he's gonna shit.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:17.900
Probably pissed- I'm sor- Hey, Slippy, I'm sorry.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:20.580
Look at his legs.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.020
Well I've missed you too, Slippy.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:25.560
Never change.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:27.640
My man.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:30.240
It's a sign of affection when they shit.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:32.600
It means they love you.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:33.220
Right?

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:35.400
[song]

